WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.520
The Blade of Calling refers to Melina as "the
one who walks alongside flame".

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.269
But what happens, if she sits alongside flame?

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:13.490
What happens...if you kill her, at the very
beginning of the game?

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.699
With Fire's Deadly Sin and the Bloodflame
glitch, this is possible.

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:21.449
Now don't worry, she doesn't stay dead, and
it doesn't ruin your game..but it does get

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:26.490
us an extremely close look at her extremely
unique death animation.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.029
With her dying breath, Melina casts one last
incantation.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:37.360
A golden erdtree erupts, and remains a while
- healing you in an AOE from all that burn

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.100
damage you took, for a small amount, over
time.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:47.320
Melina can actually cast this unique incantation
if you summon her for the fight with Morgott,

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:53.260
and she can rarely cast it during the fight
as well - not just when she dies.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:58.480
Gameplay, and lore-wise as well, this is very
similar to the spell "Blessing of the Erdtree",

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:03.030
which also heals you with the Erdtree's warmth
and grace, over time.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:08.120
And Melina, who was born at the foot of the
Erdtree, certainly has a good claim to this

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.640
powerful manifestation of its power.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.850
Even if she does feel compelled to burn it
all away.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.890
For number two,
In my last video about Miquella, we talked

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:24.100
a lot about his unalloyed gold needles, which
can be used to repel the influence of outer

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.100
gods.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:29.049
Of course, you can give a needle to Millicent,
who inserts it into her body to fight off

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:34.210
the Scarlet Rot of the Rot God..but YOU can
also use the final version of this needle..to

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:39.550
repel the influence of the outer god of frenzy,
and remove the frenzy from your eyes.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:44.490
But what you might not have known, is that
the original item description for this needle

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:49.630
originally said that "to repel the interference
of the outer god...you should pierce this

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:51.310
needle into your eyes".

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:56.619
I wonder if they changed this detail so that
they wouldn't have to create a specific animation

00:01:56.619 --> 00:01:57.710
for it?

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:58.710
Can you imagine?

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:03.520
For number 3, did you know that the winged
design of the Mausoleum Knights is clearly

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.750
inspired by the armour of the ​​winged
hussars, who were the Polish cavalry between

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.120
1503 and 1702?

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:18.950
u/FaithlessnessLucky55 shared a side-by-side
comparison of the two on Reddit and it’s

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.760
incredible to see just how similar their armor
design is.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:28.810
And it's a grand excuse to talk about why
Elden Ring and Poland decided on such extravagant

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:30.030
designs.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:35.420
In Elden Ring, the winged ornamentation of
the Mausoleum Knights is intended to evoke

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:44.930
the Deathbird, acting as a "self-inflicted
curse that ties their spirits to the land",

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:49.390
so that they might better serve their masters
in death.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:55.120
And for the polish cavalry, the rear wings
were intended to demoralize enemies during

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:02.099
their charge, as the hussars were the elite
of Polish cavalry, and not a force you would

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:04.510
want to see charging your way.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:14.651
They assembled their wings from the feathers
of raptors, birds of prey who also provide

00:03:14.651 --> 00:03:20.569
their feathers for the Ravenmount assassins
in Elden Ring, who also evoke the deathbird

00:03:20.569 --> 00:03:26.330
and have a chestpiece called the "Raptor's
Black Feathers", which states that it is "a

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:31.299
ritual implement for transforming into a Deathbird,
if only by imitation".

00:03:31.299 --> 00:03:36.730
Number 4 is something that I decided not to
include in my video on Elden Ring's cosmic

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:37.750
sorcerers.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:43.340
And it's that..Radagon shares a very compelling
connection with Raya Lucaria’s Knights of

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:49.409
the Cuckoo, who bear the twinned cuckoo bird
as their coat of arms.

00:03:49.409 --> 00:03:55.530
So... a cuckoo is a bird that lays eggs in
foreign nests so that other birds can raise

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.829
its children instead.

00:03:56.829 --> 00:04:02.659
This is something called "Brood Parasitism,”
which is… well, it’s kind of messed up

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:04.189
when you think about it.

00:04:04.189 --> 00:04:09.870
Cuckoo birds even go so far as to push eggs
and other baby birds out of the foreign nest,

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:13.500
so that there's less competition for their
own offspring.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:22.610
And..Radagon kind of exhibits this cuckoo
behaviour with Rennala.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:29.009
He uses her to birth three demigod children,
only to eventually leave her with a parting

00:04:29.009 --> 00:04:35.360
gift of a giant golden egg, which Rennala
would then treasure, seemingly at the neglect

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:40.009
of all else.

00:04:40.009 --> 00:04:44.650
And you could even take this theory further,
and argue that Radagon/Marika might have helped

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:54.960
to establish the Knights of the Cuckoo.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:05:01.789
For one, their crest is the twinned cuckoo,
which could represent the twinned body of

00:05:01.789 --> 00:05:03.000
Radagon and Marika.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:09.120
Second, the Cuckoo Surcoat item description
even says that the Cuckoo knows the insignificance

00:05:17.196 --> 00:05:23.476
as there is a legendary black moon of Nokstella
talisman that features that signature twin-cuckoo

00:05:23.476 --> 00:05:24.476
design.

00:05:24.476 --> 00:05:31.656
So you have to decide: Did Radagon/Marika
simply co-opt this ancient icon for their

00:05:31.656 --> 00:05:32.656
own purposes?

00:05:32.656 --> 00:05:39.096
Or is the cuckoo its own thing, and just coincidentally
similar to the whole situation with Radagon

00:05:39.096 --> 00:05:41.195
and Rennala's golden egg?

00:05:41.195 --> 00:05:45.686
Whatever the case, you have to admit that
it is a very compelling theory, and offers

00:05:45.686 --> 00:05:49.546
a great bit of characterisation for Radagon.

00:05:49.546 --> 00:05:58.336
This being, who only really appeared during
the war with Liurnia, as if his sole purpose

00:05:58.336 --> 00:06:03.186
was to get cose to Rennala, and undo her from
within.

00:06:03.186 --> 00:06:10.415
Another lore topic that I just keep on talking
about are the folk found all throughout Limgrave.

00:06:10.415 --> 00:06:16.005
Many of these wear the Guilty Hood which has
a description that reveals that it’s, “The

00:06:16.005 --> 00:06:21.106
garb of those accused of lesser crimes, indicated
by the collar of sharpened branches.”.

00:06:21.106 --> 00:06:28.436
But back in version 1.0 of the game, the description
read that it was the, “Garb of spurned Tarnished

00:06:28.436 --> 00:06:31.366
who were forced into slavery in the Lands
Between.”

00:06:31.366 --> 00:06:36.686
It goes on to say, “The Tarnished have been
wandering into the Lands Between from beyond

00:06:36.686 --> 00:06:40.635
the Sea of Fog in dribs and drabs since times
of old.

00:06:40.635 --> 00:06:45.616
Most are killed on arrival, but the few, unlucky
survivors are taken as slaves.”

00:06:45.616 --> 00:06:48.086
I wonder why this was changed?

00:06:48.086 --> 00:06:51.096
The 1.0 description seems so much better.

00:06:51.096 --> 00:06:56.056
For number 6, there are some interesting details
to find on the Erdtree Sentinels as well.

00:06:56.056 --> 00:07:00.075
If you look close enough at them, you’ll
notice that they’re chained to their horses.

00:07:00.075 --> 00:07:04.966
u/Groomgrim pointed out on Reddit that if
you have a look at their waist, you can see

00:07:04.966 --> 00:07:11.725
how an ornate chain wraps from around the
Sentinel, down, and around the horse.

00:07:11.725 --> 00:07:17.826
This helps to explain why, from a gameplay
point of view, they can't be dismounted like

00:07:17.826 --> 00:07:23.056
other larger enemies on horseback, such as
the Night's Cavalry.

00:07:23.056 --> 00:07:28.946
They’re truly a ride and die pair, and a
difficult one at that.

00:07:28.946 --> 00:07:33.576
One aspect of Elden Ring that isn’t talked
about very often is the game’s Hardness

00:07:33.576 --> 00:07:34.576
stat.

00:07:34.576 --> 00:07:40.075
This dictates whether or not a weapon will
bounce off an enemy when wielded with one

00:07:40.075 --> 00:07:41.075
hand.

00:07:41.075 --> 00:07:45.956
Fextralife has a helpful list explaining these
tiers, if you want to learn more.

00:07:45.956 --> 00:07:54.806
But did you know..that there's one enemy in
the game, that absolutely no weapon can match?

00:07:54.806 --> 00:07:58.306
All hail the crystal crab of Raya Lucaria.

00:07:58.306 --> 00:08:04.216
Not even the coded sword, the cipher pata,
or a whips, are a match for the hardness of

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:05.406
its shell.

00:08:05.406 --> 00:08:10.476
Another lesser-known mechanic is called "Overkill",
and it's something that you can use to massively

00:08:10.476 --> 00:08:14.105
boost the amount of runes you receive in-game.

00:08:14.105 --> 00:08:19.616
So this has been around in the Souls series
for a while, but basically, if your first

00:08:19.616 --> 00:08:27.065
hit on an enemy does damage that exceeds 150%
of their maximum HP, then you will receive

00:08:27.065 --> 00:08:33.476
20% more runes as a result.

00:08:33.476 --> 00:08:45.365
In general, this helps the rewards for fighting
to scale with the strength of your character

00:08:45.365 --> 00:08:54.485
a bit..but where tihs overkill really comes
in handy, is when you're engaging in rune

00:08:54.485 --> 00:08:55.485
farming.

00:08:55.485 --> 00:09:02.766
20% more runes is a LOT when it comes to something
like farming the albinaurics at Mohgwyn palace,

00:09:02.766 --> 00:09:07.786
so if you're currently not making use of this,
consider ways to make your character just

00:09:07.786 --> 00:09:15.646
a little more powerful, and hit that threshold.

00:09:15.646 --> 00:09:20.546
For number 9 - everyone knows about the Dectus
Medallion at this point, for having two halves

00:09:20.546 --> 00:09:24.416
of it allows for easy access to the Altus
Plateau..

00:09:24.416 --> 00:09:27.006
But did you know that's not all it does?

00:09:27.006 --> 00:09:32.685
If you have this in your inventory, it also
prevents the two guardian golems at the top,

00:09:32.685 --> 00:09:34.245
from attacking you.

00:09:34.245 --> 00:09:35.386
For number 10,

00:09:35.386 --> 00:09:38.675
Have you ever wondered why certain enemies
drop Bell Bearings?

00:09:38.675 --> 00:09:43.016
Like, what even is a bell bearing?

00:09:43.016 --> 00:09:48.166
It's a term that, as far as I can tell, doesn't
actually exist in the real world.

00:09:48.166 --> 00:09:53.766
When I first read it though, I thought it
said "Ball-bearing", which are little steel

00:09:53.766 --> 00:10:00.166
balls that go inside of an enclosure to serve
a purpose, like rolling to reduce friction,

00:10:00.166 --> 00:10:04.456
or to apply ink from a pen.

00:10:04.456 --> 00:10:11.026
So if I had to guess, a bell bearing might
be the little ball that goes inside a ball

00:10:11.026 --> 00:10:18.916
bell enclosure, so that it might function
as a "clapper" and give a bell its ring.

00:10:18.916 --> 00:10:24.356
This would make sense, as we do give these
bell bearings to the Twin Maiden husks, who

00:10:24.356 --> 00:10:31.336
are finger maidens that hold staffs that are
full of such ball bells.

00:10:31.336 --> 00:10:35.216
But why do we do this?

00:10:35.216 --> 00:10:41.566
Well, bells in the Elden Ring universe are
a tool that can be used to summon, or call

00:10:41.566 --> 00:10:43.086
to spirits.

00:10:43.086 --> 00:10:47.616
The best example of this is the spirit-calling
bell that the player uses, but this mechanic

00:10:47.616 --> 00:10:52.396
exists in other From Software games as well,
like the Bell-Ringing Women in Bloodborne,

00:10:52.396 --> 00:10:58.066
who also rings for spirits to fight on their
behalf.

00:10:58.066 --> 00:11:03.386
So when the twin maiden husks receive an NPCs
bell bearing, we [Special thanks to Quelaag

00:11:03.386 --> 00:11:07.296
for suggesting this theory] speculate that
this enables us to interact with their spirit,

00:11:07.296 --> 00:11:13.846
to learn additional spells from them, or receive
their items, as if they were still alive.

00:11:13.846 --> 00:11:20.216
After all, many bell bearings seem to hold
the essence of perished NPCs.

00:11:20.216 --> 00:11:27.946
They even might have been borne or held by
these NPCs, as many appear to have a fingerprint

00:11:27.946 --> 00:11:29.906
design upon them.

00:11:29.906 --> 00:11:38.045
So after thinking about it, the word "bell
bearing" is quite an impressively loaded phrase

00:11:38.045 --> 00:11:39.886
for these little items.

00:11:39.886 --> 00:11:48.425
It suggests that it's a part of a bell, that
it's been borne by an NPC, and that it provides

00:11:48.425 --> 00:11:55.805
a bearing, pointing one towards their spirit.

00:11:55.805 --> 00:12:03.826
Props to the translation or writing team,
for this one.

00:12:03.826 --> 00:12:10.386
So recently, twitter user Diddykolo shared
this video.

00:12:10.386 --> 00:12:16.175
It seems like this statue in the shaded castle
watches you whenever you have your back turned,

00:12:16.175 --> 00:12:19.485
only to turn away when you get closer.

00:12:19.485 --> 00:12:25.105
It's..extremely creepy - until you figure
out what's actually going on here.

00:12:25.105 --> 00:12:30.466
So after going to investigate, I realised
that this is actually being caused by textures

00:12:30.466 --> 00:12:35.846
loading in, depending on how close your character
is to them.

00:12:35.846 --> 00:12:42.266
When getting closer, it simply loads the assets
that make it look like it's looking towards

00:12:42.266 --> 00:12:43.266
you.

00:12:43.266 --> 00:12:48.115
That's not to say this isn't creepy as hell
- I remember something similar happening to

00:12:48.115 --> 00:13:00.175
me with the inanimate doll in the Hunter's
Dream of Bloodborne, and it scared the absolute

00:13:00.175 --> 00:13:05.166
hell out of me.

00:13:05.166 --> 00:13:09.766
One thing I've always wondered about is the
sequence of events that leads to you ending

00:13:09.766 --> 00:13:13.726
up in the stranded graveyard, at the beginning
of the game.

00:13:13.726 --> 00:13:28.865
Remember when you were defeated by the grafted
scion, and heard this?

00:13:28.865 --> 00:13:35.076
It's as if you're dragged..then thrown through
the air, only to be submerged underwater..and

00:13:35.076 --> 00:13:39.985
then nothing, until you finally awaken in
the Stranded Graveyard.

00:13:39.985 --> 00:13:47.946
Now what I always assumed this meant, was
that the Grafted Scion drags you, then throws

00:13:47.946 --> 00:13:50.846
you off the cliff, into the ocean below.

00:13:50.846 --> 00:13:57.516
Then, eventually, your body might wash up
towards this beach at a sort of high tide,

00:13:57.516 --> 00:14:05.105
as this beach does have a cave that leads
straight into the stranded graveyard, where

00:14:05.105 --> 00:14:07.816
Melina eventually finds you.

00:14:07.816 --> 00:14:13.766
But another theory was recently proposed by
ShieldScuff, in a youtube short that reveals

00:14:13.766 --> 00:14:19.516
that the stranded graveyard is actually right
below this crevasse in Limgrave.

00:14:19.516 --> 00:14:24.956
Falling into this crevasse usually kills you,
but if you fly the camera down there, you

00:14:24.956 --> 00:14:31.096
do arrive pretty much directly where your
character awakens.

00:14:31.096 --> 00:14:37.676
So as the theory goes, our character, and
the many piled coffins nearby, might have

00:14:37.676 --> 00:14:40.995
been hurled down here, in years passed.

00:14:40.995 --> 00:14:53.766
There's even a bunch of crucified bodies near
the hole that lends credence to this theory.

00:14:53.766 --> 00:14:59.426
The counter argument, however, is that there
isn't really a hole in the roof of the Stranded

00:14:59.426 --> 00:15:02.816
Graveyard that lines up with this crevasse.

00:15:02.816 --> 00:15:08.516
I mean..there is a tiny hole..but that's not
very convincing.

00:15:08.516 --> 00:15:18.596
There are a few caves like this with clear
holes that don't line up with the outer geography,

00:15:18.596 --> 00:15:22.006
and I think this is such a huge missed opportunity
by From Software.

00:15:22.006 --> 00:15:29.576
I reckon it would be a great little experience
to fall off a cliff only to survive, and be

00:15:29.576 --> 00:15:32.096
halfway into a dungeon.

00:15:32.096 --> 00:15:39.136
So for a long time, amongst the high-level
PvP community, people were noticing instances

00:15:39.136 --> 00:15:45.466
where they would block an attack, and perfectly
poise through it as well, without taking any

00:15:45.466 --> 00:15:46.466
knockback.

00:15:46.466 --> 00:15:54.805
Now, in PvP, and PvE, this sort of technique
could be extremely useful, because it enables

00:15:54.805 --> 00:16:04.436
the player to take no damage AND poise through
an attack in order to deliver a punish, or

00:16:04.436 --> 00:16:05.576
even a backstab.

00:16:05.576 --> 00:16:11.006
The only problem was that it wasn't known
how to replicate this seemingly random event.

00:16:11.006 --> 00:16:14.346
Or at least, it wasn't, until now...

00:16:14.346 --> 00:16:20.886
Thanks to a discovery by discord user "CMG",
and thanks to videos showcasing it by Steelovsky

00:16:20.886 --> 00:16:26.956
and JeeNiNe, we now know that to replicate
this "irregular poise event", as it's been

00:16:26.956 --> 00:16:32.456
called, what you have to do is be sprinting,
and take your finger off the sprint button,

00:16:32.456 --> 00:16:38.475
and on to the block button, in the exact frame
where you would usually take damage.

00:16:38.475 --> 00:16:44.795
This performs the perfect block with poise,
and allows you to deliver the punishing blow.

00:16:44.795 --> 00:16:50.156
I've always craved some sort of Sekiro-style
parry system in Elden Ring, so I was really

00:16:50.156 --> 00:16:52.146
excited to learn about this.

00:16:52.146 --> 00:16:56.985
It's difficult to perform, for sure, but it
really heightens the skill ceiling of the

00:16:56.985 --> 00:17:00.026
game, and that's usually a good thing.

00:17:00.026 --> 00:17:05.725
It must be hard to be a game developer and
learn about things like this - do you remove

00:17:05.725 --> 00:17:25.136
the unintended effect, or do you embrace games
having this random buggy complexity to them?

00:17:25.136 --> 00:17:30.566
Speaking of the developers, I think we should
give the animators some credit.

00:17:30.566 --> 00:17:41.546
Like..yes, they've reused a lot of animations
from previous games..but that's not being

00:17:41.546 --> 00:17:44.316
lazy, that's just being efficient.

00:17:44.316 --> 00:17:52.166
Because they clearly ton of effort into animating
so many other things instead.

00:17:52.166 --> 00:17:57.955
For example, have you considered that almost
every single enemy has a specific animation

00:17:57.955 --> 00:18:00.715
for falling, and remaining asleep?

00:18:00.715 --> 00:18:05.056
I know this isn't really a secret, I but I
feel like it still bears mentioning.

00:18:05.056 --> 00:18:14.386
Every animal, so many enemies, and bosses..all
of them have sleep effects, even if it's extremely

00:18:14.386 --> 00:18:18.686
unlikely that most players will even inflict
sleep upon them.

00:18:18.686 --> 00:18:24.046
And I bring this up, because in the recent
Miquella lore video, we talked about how there

00:18:24.046 --> 00:18:29.376
used to be a mechanic where enemies could
be found sleeping out in the world, requiring

00:18:29.376 --> 00:18:32.186
you to harvest their dream mist.

00:18:32.186 --> 00:18:41.756
So if we ever do get Miquella or St. Trina
DLC...man, it would be so smart to make it

00:18:41.756 --> 00:18:48.315
so that enemies and animals could be randomly
found sleeping around the world, so that these

00:18:48.315 --> 00:18:51.326
animations could be put to use.

00:18:51.326 --> 00:18:56.315
Speaking of sleep - have you ever looked up
during your fight with Rennala, to see where

00:18:56.315 --> 00:18:59.166
the scholars are respawning from?

00:18:59.166 --> 00:19:03.276
Turns out, they're all falling out of these
hanging cribs.

00:19:03.276 --> 00:19:09.936
We've talked before about how these beings
are rebirthed through Rennala's Great Rune

00:19:09.936 --> 00:19:37.486
of the Unborn, within "Rennala's umbra", or
shadow, so 

00:19:37.486 --> 00:19:41.955
to speak.

